# The loops over arrays of words are one linalg operation each, so their
# bodies only compute: no count changes, nothing allocated, nothing called.
# (The loop over pairs runs the library's definition as written, and the
# functions around the loops are inlined into the program's root.) The
# loops whose bodies are words alone then compute on the target's lanes;
# the maps over frozen arrays read them with a bounds check and stay loops.
idr-rc: pure-array-loops
idr-vectorize: vectorized
